# What Vercel must NOT receive.
#
# The site is plain files served as they are. The moment Vercel sees a
# package.json with a "build" script it stops serving the folder and
# tries to install and build it instead — that is what stopped every
# deploy after the bundling commit. The bundle (dist/app.js) is already
# committed, so there is nothing for Vercel to build: package.json and
# build.mjs are tools for YOUR machine only (npm run build).
package.json
package-lock.json
build.mjs
node_modules

# Working notes, tests and old copies: in the repo, never on the site.
CLAUDE.md
SECURITY.md
docs
test
_backup_pre_uid
Claude outputs
.claude
firebase.json
.firebaserc
firestore.rules
firestore.indexes.json
